<title>UK: Next stumbles on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Next stumbles on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK retailer Next Plc tumbled on Thursday, outpacing the decline in the broad market, as investors took profits, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1146 GMT, the shares were down 16-1/2p, or 2.6 percent, to 619.</p>
<p>&quot;The shares have had a good run as of late and we're just seeing some profit-taking,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>The shares had climbed 40-1/2p from February 28 to Wednesday, when they reached a fresh peak, settling at 635-1/2p. The shares added more than a pound since January 10.</p>
<p>Dealers said a few large sell orders around the 630 to 633p level precipitated the decline.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
